REM  awaz.pni — the audio cycler.  آواز
REM  A recording offers no frame to grab, so the waveform IS the picture.

CYCLER AWAZ
  TITLE   "Awaz"
  SCRIPT  "آواز"
  OUTPUT  AUDIO
  UNIT    "passage"
  PURPOSE "Make something to be heard: a song, a podcast, a lecture, an oral history, an audiobook."

  CONTRACT
    REFUSE    "a cue that ends before it starts or runs past the end"
    REFUSE    "a transcript that invents a word it could not hear"
    INVARIANT "passages are cues into one recording, never cut copies"
    EVIDENCE  "the recording sha256 in the metadata"
    EVIDENCE  "a waveform computed from the samples, not drawn"
  END CONTRACT

  REM ── Start here. Not with a recording — with what you want somebody to hear. ──

  STAGE CONCEPT
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT JSON
    INTO   book
    ASK
      I want to make something to be heard. Help me work out what it is.

      Reply with ONLY this JSON:

      {"title":"…","kind":"song|podcast|lecture|oral history|audiobook|sound work",
       "length":"how long, honestly","listener":"who is listening and while doing what",
       "voice":"whose voice, and in what register","turn":"the moment it changes",
       "done_when":"…"}

      listener: "while driving" and "with headphones, alone" are different pieces. Say which.
      turn: a recording with no turn is a file, not a work.

      What I have so far:
      {seed}
    END ASK
    VALIDATE HAS(book, "turn")
    ON FAIL CLARIFY
  END STAGE

  STAGE RUNNING
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   book
    INTO   book.running
    ASK
      Write the running order in 80 to 150 words: what is heard, in sequence, with rough
      durations. Mark where the turn falls.

      If this is speech, say who speaks and whether anyone answers. If it is music, say what
      the arrangement is. If it is neither, describe the sound.
    END ASK
  END STAGE


  STAGE PASSAGES
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT LIST
    INTO   passages
    ASK
      A recording from "{book}", {duration} long. Divide it into passages.

      Reply with ONLY a JSON array, in order:
      [{"start":"0:00","end":"1:20","title":"…","beat":"…"}]

      beat: what changes there — a key, a speaker, a section, a turn in the argument.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COUNT(passages) > 0
  END STAGE

  STAGE TRANSCRIBE
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   MEASURE
    EXPECT TEXT
    OPTIONAL
    REPEAT FOREACH passages
    INTO   passage.transcript
    ASK
      Transcribe passage {passage.title}, {passage.start} to {passage.end}. Verbatim.
      Mark each speaker if there is more than one. Mark [inaudible] where it is, and
      do not guess at it. Where it is not speech, describe what is heard in one line.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE HEARD
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   passage.transcript
    INTO   passage.lead
    ASK
      Passage {passage.title}, {passage.start} to {passage.end}.
      ONE paragraph of 50 to 90 words describing what is heard, in the vocabulary the
      recording itself uses.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE WORDS(passage.lead) >= 40
  END STAGE

  STAGE LISTENFOR
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   passage.lead
    INTO   passage.explanation
    ASK
      Same passage. Name the one thing a listener should attend to and why it carries
      the passage. Preserve any hedging the recording uses. 50 to 90 words.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE ABSTRACT
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   INTEGRATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   passages
    INTO   book.description
    ASK
      Deposit abstract for "{book}", a recording of {duration} in {count} passages.
      Two or three HTML paragraphs in <p> tags.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE MINT
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB  INTEGRATE
    GATE  HUMAN "MINT awaz"
    EMIT  DOI
  END STAGE
END CYCLER
